%% review-flight-deck level 2 — one run, event to merged bundle
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant T as Workflow
    participant F as flightdeck mode
    participant H as GitHub
    participant G as local git
    actor R as Reviewer
    participant L as ledger.py
    participant N as path runner

    T->>F: pull_request event
    F->>H: list open pull requests
    H-->>F: 17 open, 5 already auto-merged
    F->>F: 8 have no description
    F->>F: run generate mode for those 8
    F->>G: merge-base of every open head
    G-->>F: 0c099be, the common ancestor

    F->>F: simulate 3 paths from that base
    loop best 1 or 2 paths only
        F->>G: replay the bundles on a scratch worktree
        G-->>F: conflicts, or clean
    end
    F->>F: classify what no path can carry
    F-->>R: one validated path, 10 in, 2 held out

    R->>R: read the outcome, then the contributions
    R->>L: append path_accept, with the rollout choice
    L->>L: write one line, rebuild the projection

    loop one bundle at a time
        N->>L: read the next unmerged bundle
        N->>H: merge the bundle onto flightdeck/path-a/N
        N-->>R: checkpoint, a tree to check out
        R->>L: append merge_bundle for the next one
    end
    N->>H: open one pull request onto the default branch
